      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The hexagon consists of six equilateral triangles of side \\(10.\\) Its area is \\[ 6\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\cdot10^2\\right) =150\\sqrt3 \\] square inches.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "An inscribed regular hexagon has side length equal to the circle’s radius",
        "Divide the hexagon into six equilateral triangles of side \\(10\\)"
